{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The custom GEMM does not beat the tuned ROCm library on large workloads. I found PyTorch’s grouped-GEMM entry point, which could launch both products together; I’m testing whether its one unavoidable cost—packing the two independently supplied weight tensors—can be made cheap enough to win overall."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch\nK=3072\nw1=torch.randn((K,K),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16);w2=torch.randn_like(w1)\n\ndef bench(fn,n):\n for _ in range(5):fn()\n torch.cuda.synchronize();a=torch.cuda.Event(True);z=torch.cuda.Event(True);a.record()\n for _ in range(n):fn()\n z.record();z.synchronize();return a.elapsed_time(z)*1000/n\nfor m in (128,613,8192,17312):\n h=torch.randn((3,m,K),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16);x=h[1:]\n wt=torch.stack((w1,w2),0).transpose(1,2)\n dst=torch.empty((2,K,K),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\n def foreach_copy():\n  torch._foreach_copy_((dst[0],dst[1]),(w1,w2))\n def pair_copy():\n  dst[0].copy_(w1);dst[1].copy_(w2)\n def grouped(): return torch._grouped_mm(x,wt,out_dtype=torch.float32)\n def bmm():return torch.bmm(x,wt,out_dtype=torch.float32)\n n=100 if m<1000 else 20\n print('M',m,'grouped',bench(grouped,n),'bmm',bench(bmm,n),'foreachcopy',bench(foreach_copy,n),'paircopy',bench(pair_copy,n))\n q=grouped();r=bmm();torch.cuda.synchronize();print('diff', (q-r).abs().max().item())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
