{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The single-launch small-M kernel is a clear win locally: about 33–37 µs for 128–256 rows and 47–50 µs for 422–613 rows, versus roughly 45–61 µs with library calls. Its FP32 accumulators are even closer numerically than the BF16 shortcut. I’ve wired it for all five small row counts and am running the penultimate official check."}}
